; Cultivated field — TerrainDefinition data entry (spec.md -> Data Schemas; terrain.md ->
; Already-Defined Terrain, v1 tag-source mapping).
;
; emitted_tags = ["cultivated"] is DECIDED (terrain.md's tag-source mapping, #5 closed ->
; D-25). This is the villager's habitat terrain: carrying capacity counts cultivated tiles
; in radius to decide how many families a House supports, which is why cultivated ships at
; the floor rather than as depth.
;
; cost = 2 is DECIDED 2026-08-01 (-> D-29), at terrain.md's stated baseline ("~2 Wood /
; tile — fencing & tools", Open Question #8 closed). It is the only non-zero terrain cost
; in v1 and therefore the only place terrain.md's pricing rule ("nature is free;
; construction costs materials") has any teeth.
;
; Not harvestable: `land_use = cultivated` exists in the HarvestableTileDefinition schema
; for the deferred multi-resource system, but no v1 crop yields anything (terrain.md names
; Forest as v1's SOLE harvestable).
;
; MODEL_SCENE NOW POINTS AT REAL ART (2026-08-16): 2 variants, both newly sourced and
; imported this pass — CultivatedWheatRow.tscn (Wheat.glb, 6-clump furrow arrangement) and
; CultivatedCropsPlot.tscn (CropsPlot.glb, a pre-composed 5-row plot). Human complaint:
; "needs to look like actual farm fields" — both compose a small plot with visible rows,
; not a single plant in a box. New source pack: Nature/Crops assets individually sourced
; via poly.pizza — project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres (CC0).
; See each .tscn's own header for scale/composition reasoning. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF —
; same as every other terrain in this pass.
;
; MODEL_SCENE PLURALIZED TO MODEL_SCENES (-> D-42): the field is now an array so a
; terrain can carry multiple interchangeable visual variants, stably picked per tile by
; TerrainDefinition.pick_variant().
;
; 24 PER-SPECIES CROP VARIANTS ADDED (2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 7): 8 species
; (Wheat, Corn, Carrot, Lettuce, Tomato, Pumpkin, Apple, Cactus) x 3 variants each (a
; mid-growth "_2" frame, a full-grown "_4" frame, and a post-harvest-reading 3rd variant —
; the cap confirmed with the human at 2 growth stages + 1 harvested per species), 24 new
; model_scenes entries total (2 -> 26). Source: "Nature Crops Pack" (Jan 2020) by
; Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_nature_crops_pack.tres. This is a DIFFERENT
; source than CultivatedWheatRow/CultivatedCropsPlot above (those used individually
; poly.pizza-downloaded "Wheat"/"Crops" models, quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres) — this
; pack is an on-disk named/dated pack extraction, the same sourcing shape as the Ultimate
; Nature Pack (quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres), so it gets its own attribution file
; rather than extending either existing one.
;
; AUDIT FINDING BEYOND THE BRIEF: the brief's table said only Carrot lacks a "_Harvested"
; file (use "_Crop" instead). On-disk verification found WHEAT ALSO LACKS "_Harvested" —
; same substitution applied (CropWheatCrop.tscn uses Wheat_Crop.fbx). Every other species
; (Corn, Lettuce, Tomato, Pumpkin, Apple, Cactus) does ship a real "_Harvested" file, used
; as specified.
;
; MEASUREMENT-TOOLING GOTCHA (applies to all 24 new scenes, recorded once here rather than
; repeated in every header): the one-off SceneTree AABB script used to measure each raw
; FBX's height/footprint initially reported implausibly tiny numbers (~0.001 tile-units)
; because Node3D.global_transform silently returns Transform3D.IDENTITY when the node
; hasn't actually been marked is_inside_tree() yet inside a --script SceneTree run's
; _init() — which was the case here even after add_child(). This pack's raw FBX meshes
; each carry a baked ~100x scale + 90-degree Y/Z-swap axis-correction transform on their
; MeshInstance3D's LOCAL `transform` (a normal FBX up-axis artifact); the silent-identity
; fallback hid that transform entirely and produced bogus (and, for Wheat, direction-
; reversed) measurements. Fixed by manually composing each node's local `transform` from
; the instanced root down to the mesh, not by reading global_transform. Re-verify this if
; any future pass reuses the same measurement-script pattern against a new FBX pack.
;
; SCALE (measured via the corrected script above): each of the 24 items was scaled to a
; per-role target — mid "~0.10 tile-units tall", grown "~0.16", harvested-reading
; "~0.07" — capped by a max-footprint-axis limit (0.22/0.30/0.20 respectively) so wide/
; short models (Cactus, Lettuce, Pumpkin) don't overrun the tile once scaled to their
; target height. 3 small clustered instances per tile (not a single plant in the middle of
; a box), same per-instance rotation+scale jitter convention CultivatedWheatRow's 6 clumps
; already established. Per-item raw AABB and computed target are recorded in each item's
; own .tscn header. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF — same posture as every other scale/count
; decision in this pass: the stage choice ("_2"/"_4" over "_1"/"_3"), the per-role target
; heights, the 3-instance cluster count, and the Wheat/Carrot "_Crop" substitution are all
; first-pass judgment calls pending an in-engine eyeball pass.
;
; WHAT "FOOTPRINT CAPPED" MEANS IN ALL 24 HEADERS (recorded once here, 2026-08-26 final
; whole-branch review, rather than restated in every scene): the cap is measured on the
; model's AXIS-ALIGNED footprint BEFORE the per-instance rotation jitter each scene applies.
; A rotated axis-aligned box reads wider on its diagonal — up to ~1.19x at 45 degrees — so a
; post-jitter measurement of a "capped at 0.30" item can legitimately come back at ~0.36.
; That is expected geometry, not a cap overrun: every capped value still leaves the
; instance comfortably inside the 1x1 tile even at the worst-case diagonal, since the caps
; (0.22/0.30/0.20) are well under the 0.5 tile half-footprint the clustered offsets work
; against. Read a header's cap number as a pre-jitter control on the raw model's scale, not
; as a claim about the shipped instance's world-space AABB.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TerrainDefinition" load_steps=28 format=3]

